// XFAIL: RT-439: a generic type alias as an expression path without its arguments, `type OV<T> = Option<T>;` then `OV::Some(&d)`, is refused: "type alias 'OV' is generic: write its type arguments"; rustc infers them and prints the EXPECT lines (0.30.2)
// From the paused g302temps work (PAUSED.md, findings not yet reported:
// "a generic type alias in an expression path errors either way", form
// c06). Since v0.30.1 at least (the same error).
